    # The places Calebais prints as headings: the village and the wood (Chapter One), the ruins of Calebais, its
    # levels and their rooms (Chapter Two), the convent (Chapter Three). The book fixes no geography (it offers
    # three Tribunals to set it in, p6), so the four stand at the top. TAGS: place, level or room. A place's text
    # is in its chapter's .lore, under its heading.

